{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VUh3gfWbytnrmuDgr6Qn4a","type":"tool_result","content":"18:# the per-run control dispatches each loop's signal files through its adapter\n411:# pid is not alive — a numeric pid that `kill -0` cannot signal, or a missing/\n497:# Classify a worker's health from progress signals so the dashboard can surface a\n558:# empty, 1 when the last line is unique). A long run is the loop signal.\n768:# pure-ish file/signal operations (no gum, no menu), so they are unit-testable and\n772:# Map a run type + signal kind to the dot-file basename the loop's runner watches\n773:# for between rounds. Thin pass-through to almanac_loop_signal_file (lib/loops.sh),\n778:almanac_loop_run_signal_file() {\n779:  almanac_loop_signal_file \"$1\" \"$2\"\n783:# the type's stop|steer dot-file basename (`<base>/.harden-stop`, …). Centralises\n784:# the harden/converge pattern of \"look up the signal file, prepend the path\" so\n790:  name=\"$(almanac_loop_run_signal_file \"$type\" \"$kind\")\" || return 1\n797:# host PID signaling, so hub stop never sends TERM from a recorded pid. Returns 2\n812:  stop_file=\"$(almanac_loop_run_signal_file \"$type\" stop)\" || return 3\n835:  steer_file=\"$(almanac_loop_run_signal_file \"$type\" steer)\" || return 3","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01G1XmY5XvTbbUFYvBrgo6G5","session_id":"3ef28929-b60b-453b-bba1-b6ef6c6d207d","uuid":"4100c3fa-f3c3-4367-885b-dbab3e18423f","timestamp":"2026-05-27T07:03:41.457Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Codebase friction exploration"}
