{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFxw9GspPy1NAWdEc9VPaw","type":"tool_result","content":"13:#   control — signal_file <stop|steer>: its between-round dot-file basename.\n14:#             Optional override — almanac_loop_default_signal_file (below) handles\n17:#             through almanac_loop_signal_file (consumed by lib/run.sh control).\n98:# Default signal-file basename for a loop's between-round control. Every loop uses\n101:# only needs to define its own `signal_file` if its convention diverges; this is\n104:almanac_loop_default_signal_file() {\n112:# Resolve a loop's signal-file basename: the adapter's override if it defines\n113:# `signal_file`, else the standard `.${name}-${kind}` default. This is the\n116:# loop costs zero signal_file code unless the loop is non-standard. Returns 1 for\n118:almanac_loop_signal_file() {\n122:  fn=\"almanac_loop_${key}_signal_file\"\n126:    almanac_loop_default_signal_file \"$key\" \"$2\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01G1XmY5XvTbbUFYvBrgo6G5","session_id":"3ef28929-b60b-453b-bba1-b6ef6c6d207d","uuid":"ba65ac5f-df35-4ae3-9aed-4b7744be498a","timestamp":"2026-05-27T07:03:43.080Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Codebase friction exploration"}
