{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qe7MCBezuVhrMuMr6arFut","type":"tool_result","content":"1670\t    if [ \"$round_rc\" -eq 0 ] && almanac_harden_acceptance_met \"$rubric_path\"; then\n1671\t      acc=1\n1672\t    fi\n1673\t\n1674\t    verdict=\"$(almanac_harden_gate_verdict \"$acc\" \"$open_count\" \"$round\" \"$budget\")\" && rc=0 || rc=$?\n1675\t    if [ \"$acc\" -eq 1 ]; then acc_label=\"met\"; else acc_label=\"unmet\"; fi\n1676\t    _info \"Verdict: $verdict (round $round/$budget, open-blocking=$open_count, acceptance=$acc_label)\"\n1677\t\n1678\t    case \"$rc\" in\n1679\t      0)\n1680\t        _success \"Converged after $round round(s): acceptance met and no open blocking findings remain.\"\n1681\t        almanac_harden_run_finalize \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"done\"\n1682\t        return 0\n1683\t        ;;\n1684\t      2)\n1685\t        _warn \"Round budget ($budget) reached — $open_count open blocking finding(s) remain. Status: NON-CONVERGED.\"\n1686\t        almanac_harden_run_finalize \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"failed\"\n1687\t        return 1\n1688\t        ;;\n1689\t      *)\n1690\t        # HITL checkpoint: continue, ship, or steer. A steer (rc 2) echoes the\n1691\t        # new directive on stdout; capture it and thread it into the next round.\n1692\t        steer_directive=\"$(almanac_harden_hitl_checkpoint)\" && hitl_rc=0 || hitl_rc=$?\n1693\t        case \"$hitl_rc\" in\n1694\t          2)\n1695\t            directive=\"$steer_directive\"\n1696\t            if [ -n \"$directive\" ]; then\n1697\t              _info \"Steering applied for the next round: $directive\"\n1698\t            else\n1699\t              _info \"Steering directive cleared for the next round.\"\n1700\t            fi\n1701\t            continue\n1702\t            ;;\n1703\t          0)\n1704\t            continue\n1705\t            ;;\n1706\t          *)\n1707\t            _success \"Shipping at round $round by request — $open_count open blocking finding(s) left unaddressed.\"\n1708\t            almanac_harden_run_finalize \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"done\"\n1709\t            return 0\n1710\t            ;;\n1711\t        esac\n1712\t        ;;\n1713\t    esac\n1714\t  done\n1715\t}\n1716\t\n1717\t# --- Supervision dashboard -----------------------------------------------------\n1718\t#\n1719\t# A gum-styled redraw dashboard for supervising a harden run: reviewer status (per\n1720\t# lens, with health), the round, findings tallies, rubric progress, and the\n1721\t# feedback verdict. The render LOGIC is pure (almanac_harden_dashboard_rows: state\n1722\t# -> printable rows) so it is unit-testable without a terminal; the gather helpers\n1723\t# read live run state into that pure composer, and almanac_harden_render_dashboard\n1724\t# wraps the result in gum styling that degrades to plain output when gum is absent\n1725\t# (via the shared UI primitives in lib/ui.sh).\n1726\t\n1727\t# Findings tally for the dashboard: counts the ledger's findings by status as\n1728\t# `open=N fixed=N notes=N`, where notes = rejected-subjective + wontfix-per-context\n1729\t# (the non-blocking outcomes). Prints all-zero when the ledger is absent."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ef28929-b60b-453b-bba1-b6ef6c6d207d","uuid":"81909c5b-d0bf-493c-8985-7870f7d1ec26","timestamp":"2026-05-27T07:05:11.513Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/harden-core.sh","content":"    if [ \"$round_rc\" -eq 0 ] && almanac_harden_acceptance_met \"$rubric_path\"; then\n      acc=1\n    fi\n\n    verdict=\"$(almanac_harden_gate_verdict \"$acc\" \"$open_count\" \"$round\" \"$budget\")\" && rc=0 || rc=$?\n    if [ \"$acc\" -eq 1 ]; then acc_label=\"met\"; else acc_label=\"unmet\"; fi\n    _info \"Verdict: $verdict (round $round/$budget, open-blocking=$open_count, acceptance=$acc_label)\"\n\n    case \"$rc\" in\n      0)\n        _success \"Converged after $round round(s): acceptance met and no open blocking findings remain.\"\n        almanac_harden_run_finalize \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"done\"\n        return 0\n        ;;\n      2)\n        _warn \"Round budget ($budget) reached — $open_count open blocking finding(s) remain. Status: NON-CONVERGED.\"\n        almanac_harden_run_finalize \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"failed\"\n        return 1\n        ;;\n      *)\n        # HITL checkpoint: continue, ship, or steer. A steer (rc 2) echoes the\n        # new directive on stdout; capture it and thread it into the next round.\n        steer_directive=\"$(almanac_harden_hitl_checkpoint)\" && hitl_rc=0 || hitl_rc=$?\n        case \"$hitl_rc\" in\n          2)\n            directive=\"$steer_directive\"\n            if [ -n \"$directive\" ]; then\n              _info \"Steering applied for the next round: $directive\"\n            else\n              _info \"Steering directive cleared for the next round.\"\n            fi\n            continue\n            ;;\n          0)\n            continue\n            ;;\n          *)\n            _success \"Shipping at round $round by request — $open_count open blocking finding(s) left unaddressed.\"\n            almanac_harden_run_finalize \"$root\" \"$run_id\" \"done\"\n            return 0\n            ;;\n        esac\n        ;;\n    esac\n  done\n}\n\n# --- Supervision dashboard -----------------------------------------------------\n#\n# A gum-styled redraw dashboard for supervising a harden run: reviewer status (per\n# lens, with health), the round, findings tallies, rubric progress, and the\n# feedback verdict. The render LOGIC is pure (almanac_harden_dashboard_rows: state\n# -> printable rows) so it is unit-testable without a terminal; the gather helpers\n# read live run state into that pure composer, and almanac_harden_render_dashboard\n# wraps the result in gum styling that degrades to plain output when gum is absent\n# (via the shared UI primitives in lib/ui.sh).\n\n# Findings tally for the dashboard: counts the ledger's findings by status as\n# `open=N fixed=N notes=N`, where notes = rejected-subjective + wontfix-per-context\n# (the non-blocking outcomes). Prints all-zero when the ledger is absent.","numLines":60,"startLine":1670,"totalLines":1978}}}
