{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01EbRD5GTPK6eUwYFJ54YVBB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHFHSkoXr7eTL4WiieUmgD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nrefactor(run): drop pass-through signal_file wrapper, harden converge resume\n\nThree small architectural fixes to the run-registry layer:\n\n1. Delete the shallow almanac_loop_run_signal_file wrapper in lib/run.sh.\n   It was a single-line pass-through to almanac_loop_signal_file with no\n   added behaviour — deletion test passes cleanly. Three internal callers\n   in run.sh now call the loop-adapter seam directly.\n\n2. Extend the canonical run-status schema with goal/prompt/exec/oversee_every\n   so converge runs persist enough config for the hub's resume path to\n   rebuild the launch command from status.tsv. Pre-fix, `status_to_opts`\n   read these fields but the converge runner never wrote them — resume\n   silently dropped --goal and the action verb. Tests for status_to_opts\n   existed but failed silently because set_run_config rejected the\n   non-canonical keys (test-run.sh wasn't runnable on macOS bash 3.2;\n   see #3).\n\n3. Replace `mapfile -t` in tests/test-run.sh with a portable\n   `split_lines_into` helper. `mapfile` is bash 4+; macOS ships bash 3.2,\n   so the round-trip resume tests were unreachable on the dev host.\n\nAlso: add three convergence.md outcome regression tests (FAILED on hard\nexec failure; NON_CONVERGED on --no-oversee budget exhaustion;\nplus existing CONVERGED/NON_CONVERGED/STOPPED) — pin the outcome /\nlast-verdict split introduced in 19e787a so it can't silently regress.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit the bundle"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1430,"cache_read_input_tokens":170655,"cache_creation":{