{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CAuoRV6nRY5TwAbvdfmwdq","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 19e787a28d1f91ba8acf4dcb21a3d77860e58d63\nAuthor: Jakub <neumie@neumie.dev>\nDate:   Wed May 27 09:10:17 2026 +0200\n\n    fix(converge): convergence.md splits outcome from last verdict\n    \n    Bug: a converge run that hit its round budget without convergence wrote\n    \"Final verdict: CONTINUE\" — readable as a soft answer, actually meaning\n    \"the overseer wanted more rounds and we ran out of budget\". Observed in\n    docs/plans/converge/run-the-prompt-…/convergence.md:\n    \n      ## Final verdict\n      CONTINUE              ← LLM-overseer last said \"go around again\"\n      ## Tick count\n      10                    ← matched the 10-round budget → run terminated\n      ## Final reason\n      none                  ← empty (REASON parser bug, fixed in c85b749)\n    \n    A new converge run reading that file misread it as \"the system decided\n    this is done; don't duplicate the prior settled work\". Wrong — the loop\n    never converged; it ran out of attempts.\n    \n    Fix: introduce an authoritative `outcome` field separate from the raw\n    last-overseer verdict. Five outcomes cover every termination path:\n    \n      CONVERGED       overseer said so → goal met\n      NON_CONVERGED   round budget hit before convergence\n      STOPPED         stop signal (overseer STOP verdict OR human .converge-stop)\n      FAILED          exec error with CONVERGE_FAIL_ON_EXEC_ERROR=1\n      ABORTED         EXIT trap (mid-loop _die, signal)\n    \n    Each comes with a one-line headline so future operators / agents can act\n    on it without parsing the rest:\n    \n      ## Outcome\n      NON_CONVERGED — round budget exhausted (10/10) without overseer reaching CONVERGED.\n    \n      ## Last overseer verdict\n      CONTINUE                 ← informational; not a final answer\n    \n      ## Tick count\n      10 of 10                 ← now shows consumed-of-budget\n    \n      ## Termination reason\n      round budget (10) exhausted; overseer's last verdict was CONTINUE\n    \n    The split makes the misread structurally impossible: `outcome` is the\n    authoritative result, `last verdict` is metadata. An agent reading\n    convergence.md can't conflate \"Last overseer verdict: CONTINUE\" with\n    \"the system decided we're done\" — those live in separate sections with\n    different field names.\n    \n    Implementation:\n      - `almanac_converge_write_convergence` takes a new signature:\n        (root, goal, outcome, last_verdict, tick, budget, started, reason).\n      - `almanac_converge_run` tracks `final_outcome` alongside the existing\n        `final_status` / `final_verdict` / `final_reason`. Defaults to\n        NON_CONVERGED at loop entry (the budget-exhaustion case); promoted\n        to CONVERGED / STOPPED inside the overseer-verdict switch; or to\n        FAILED on the exec-error early-exit path.\n      - Stop-signal path also sets `final_outcome=STOPPED` (was: relied on\n        final_verdict=\"STOP\" which conflated outcome with verdict).\n      - The signature also gains the budget field so the convergence.md\n        can render \"10 of 10\" instead of just \"10\" — makes \"ran out of\n        attempts\" visually obvious.\n    \n    Tests:\n      - Existing test for CONVERGED verdict updated for the new section\n        names (Outcome, Last overseer verdict, Termination reason).\n      - New regression test for NON_CONVERGED labeling: drive 3 rounds with\n        a fake overseer that always says CONTINUE, assert convergence.md\n        contains NON_CONVERGED and \"round budget exhausted\" — the exact\n        misread scenario from the original bug.\n      - New regression test for STOPPED: STOP verdict outcome=STOPPED.\n    \n    All 17 converge tests pass.\n    \n    Note: test-run.sh::test_status_to_opts_inverts_ralph_status fails on\n    macOS bash 3.2 because it uses `mapfile` (bash 4+ only) — but that\n    failure pre-dates this commit (introduced in aad12c68 by the previous\n    converge run). Surfaced as a separate follow-up.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n tests/test-converge.sh | 124 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n 1 file changed, 119 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n---\ncommit b0d93291c499b0808075637880387cbe586efba5\nAuthor: Jakub <neumie@neumie.dev>\nDate:   Wed May 27 09:06:52 2026 +0200\n\n    fix(converge): split final_outcome from last verdict in convergence.md\n    \n    Authoritative termination shape is the outcome (CONVERGED/NON_CONVERGED/\n    STOPPED/FAILED), not the overseer's last verdict. Budget exhaustion used\n    to render as \"Final verdict: CONTINUE\" — misread by future agents as a\n    soft stop. Outcome now reports NON_CONVERGED with the verdict listed\n    separately as informational.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n lib/converge-core.sh | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++------\n 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ef28929-b60b-453b-bba1-b6ef6c6d207d","uuid":"4c7cc1a8-a84c-4918-85ed-16434df7c99f","timestamp":"2026-05-27T07:31:30.467Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 19e787a28d1f91ba8acf4dcb21a3d77860e58d63\nAuthor: Jakub <neumie@neumie.dev>\nDate:   Wed May 27 09:10:17 2026 +0200\n\n    fix(converge): convergence.md splits outcome from last verdict\n    \n    Bug: a converge run that hit its round budget without convergence wrote\n    \"Final verdict: CONTINUE\" — readable as a soft answer, actually meaning\n    \"the overseer wanted more rounds and we ran out of budget\". Observed in\n    docs/plans/converge/run-the-prompt-…/convergence.md:\n    \n      ## Final verdict\n      CONTINUE              ← LLM-overseer last said \"go around again\"\n      ## Tick count\n      10                    ← matched the 10-round budget → run terminated\n      ## Final reason\n      none                  ← empty (REASON parser bug, fixed in c85b749)\n    \n    A new converge run reading that file misread it as \"the system decided\n    this is done; don't duplicate the prior settled work\". Wrong — the loop\n    never converged; it ran out of attempts.\n    \n    Fix: introduce an authoritative `outcome` field separate from the raw\n    last-overseer verdict. Five outcomes cover every termination path:\n    \n      CONVERGED       overseer said so → goal met\n      NON_CONVERGED   round budget hit before convergence\n      STOPPED         stop signal (overseer STOP verdict OR human .converge-stop)\n      FAILED          exec error with CONVERGE_FAIL_ON_EXEC_ERROR=1\n      ABORTED         EXIT trap (mid-loop _die, signal)\n    \n    Each comes with a one-line headline so future operators / agents can act\n    on it without parsing the rest:\n    \n      ## Outcome\n      NON_CONVERGED — round budget exhausted (10/10) without overseer reaching CONVERGED.\n    \n      ## Last overseer verdict\n      CONTINUE                 ← informational; not a final answer\n    \n      ## Tick count\n      10 of 10                 ← now shows consumed-of-budget\n    \n      ## Termination reason\n      round budget (10) exhausted; overseer's last verdict was CONTINUE\n    \n    The split makes the misread structurally impossible: `outcome` is the\n    authoritative result, `last verdict` is metadata. An agent reading\n    convergence.md can't conflate \"Last overseer verdict: CONTINUE\" with\n    \"the system decided we're done\" — those live in separate sections with\n    different field names.\n    \n    Implementation:\n      - `almanac_converge_write_convergence` takes a new signature:\n        (root, goal, outcome, last_verdict, tick, budget, started, reason).\n      - `almanac_converge_run` tracks `final_outcome` alongside the existing\n        `final_status` / `final_verdict` / `final_reason`. Defaults to\n        NON_CONVERGED at loop entry (the budget-exhaustion case); promoted\n        to CONVERGED / STOPPED inside the overseer-verdict switch; or to\n        FAILED on the exec-error early-exit path.\n      - Stop-signal path also sets `final_outcome=STOPPED` (was: relied on\n        final_verdict=\"STOP\" which conflated outcome with verdict).\n      - The signature also gains the budget field so the convergence.md\n        can render \"10 of 10\" instead of just \"10\" — makes \"ran out of\n        attempts\" visually obvious.\n    \n    Tests:\n      - Existing test for CONVERGED verdict updated for the new section\n        names (Outcome, Last overseer verdict, Termination reason).\n      - New regression test for NON_CONVERGED labeling: drive 3 rounds with\n        a fake overseer that always says CONTINUE, assert convergence.md\n        contains NON_CONVERGED and \"round budget exhausted\" — the exact\n        misread scenario from the original bug.\n      - New regression test for STOPPED: STOP verdict outcome=STOPPED.\n    \n    All 17 converge tests pass.\n    \n    Note: test-run.sh::test_status_to_opts_inverts_ralph_status fails on\n    macOS bash 3.2 because it uses `mapfile` (bash 4+ only) — but that\n    failure pre-dates this commit (introduced in aad12c68 by the previous\n    converge run). Surfaced as a separate follow-up.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n tests/test-converge.sh | 124 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n 1 file changed, 119 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n---\ncommit b0d93291c499b0808075637880387cbe586efba5\nAuthor: Jakub <neumie@neumie.dev>\nDate:   Wed May 27 09:06:52 2026 +0200\n\n    fix(converge): split final_outcome from last verdict in convergence.md\n    \n    Authoritative termination shape is the outcome (CONVERGED/NON_CONVERGED/\n    STOPPED/FAILED), not the overseer's last verdict. Budget exhaustion used\n    to render as \"Final verdict: CONTINUE\" — misread by future agents as a\n    soft stop. Outcome now reports NON_CONVERGED with the verdict listed\n    separately as informational.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n lib/converge-core.sh | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++------\n 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
